1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,920
Thirty thousand euros.

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,760
Four community commitments.

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:06,220
No plan that can satisfy them all.

4
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:10,400
Common Ground makes that conflict visible, before anyone builds.

5
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,520
Here, residents set the budget and minimums for shade, access,

6
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,200
play and rain.

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,520
These are illustrative design points, not measured impacts.

8
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:22,990
The studio checks all four thousand and ninety-six combinations

9
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,970
of twelve interventions.

10
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:28,210
At thirty thousand, the commitments cannot all hold.

11
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:33,140
Inspect the certificate: budget, shade, access and rain form

12
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,080
an irreducible conflict.

13
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,760
We could lower a target.

14
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,120
Or change the budget.

15
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:42,230
Seven thousand euros more preserves every original minimum.

16
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,630
One plan survives.

17
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:45,150
A grove of trees.

18
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:46,530
An accessible loop.

19
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:47,890
A wildflower patch.

20
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:49,270
A table for everyone.

21
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,300
The result is something you can take away.

22
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,320
Export the proposal, then open the actual file.

23
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:57,770
The reader reruns the full search.

24
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:01,450
Costs, commitments and the selected plan agree.

25
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:04,670
Change the saved result, and verification fails.

26
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:09,120
The next step is a real workshop, with local costs and residents.

27
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,460
Common Ground.

28
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:12,100
Make the compromise visible.
